# Negative test (issue #458, migrated for the single syntax): the unit value
# where an integer is expected is a conversion failure naming the unit type.
# (Under the old .ep syntax this case was `proc one : Int = 1`, where bare
# `1` was the unit type; under the single syntax `1` is the integer literal
# and the unit value is spelled `unitv`.)
postulate(Int, Univ)
proc one : Int = unitv
